by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes."," - 2026-10-10 — refresh under approval. Copied: low-level-requirements.toml (ref: WI-880); test-cases.toml (ref: WI-880). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes.","+- 2026-10-10 — refresh under approval. Copied: system-requirements.toml (re-attested: SR-019, SR-020, SR-032, SR-046). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes."]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-880\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":572,"oldLines":3,"newStart":572,"newLines":9,"lines":[" date = \"2026-10-10\""," approved = [\"LLR-326\", \"TC-350\"]"," reattested = []","+","+[[act]]","+seq = 95","+date = \"2026-10-10\"","+approved = []","+reattested = [\"SR-019\", \"SR-020\", \"SR-032\", \"SR-046\"]"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-880\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\system-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":117,"oldLines":7,"newStart":117,"newLines":7,"lines":[" hat_refs = [\"SECURITY\"]"," requirement = \"\"\"The pre-commit hook shall run the integrity + secrets floor on every commit, agent-neutrally — a LOCAL floor, bypassable by the session (git commit --no-verify), so it discharges \"no unchecked write enters governed state\" only as a PAIR with the hosted re-run of the same bar (SR-151/SR-152), never alone.\"\"\""," rationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-005 and SN-009 — a floor only CI enforces is one the local tree crosses freely, and a secret caught after the commit is already in history. Trusting the agent to run the checks was rejected: a floor exists for the times the agent forgets, so it is git-enforced and agent-neutral. Parents the interpreter probe: a hook that crashes cryptically because no python3 resolves, or because a Windows Store alias exits nonzero, has not run the floor — so probing by RUNNING a candidate and reporting clearly is machinery serving THIS obligation, and it decomposes to LLR-021 rather than standing as a requirement of its own.\"\"\"","-acceptance_criteria = \"\"\"The hook runs the registry-integrity floor and the secrets scan on staged content and blocks a commit that fails either; a --no-verify commit bypasses it and is caught instead by the hosted re-run, which is what makes the pair — not this row — the honest unit of the claim.\"\"\"","+acceptance_criteria = \"The hook runs the registry-integrity floor and the secrets scan on staged content and blocks a commit that fails either. With no interpreter at the runtime floor, the commit hooks refuse the commit, name the developer-setup install step, and neither run the floor below that floor nor skip it. A --no-verify commit bypasses the hook and is caught instead by the hosted re-run, which is what makes the pair - not this row - the honest unit of the claim.\""," priority = \"M\""," verification = \"Test\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":131,"oldLines":7,"newStart":131,"newLines":7,"lines":[" hat_refs = [\"DATA-PROTECTION\", \"SECURITY\"]"," requirement = \"\"\"The pre-push hook shall scan the outgoing commit range and block a push that publishes a secret or (under privacy-check) a private identity.\"\"\""," rationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-005 and SN-009 — the last gate before content leaves the machine. Parents the interpreter probe, with SR-019: LLR-021 is declared on this hook's module, and a pre-push hook that cannot start scans nothing. The probe is mechanism, not a second obligation.\"\"\"","-acceptance_criteria = \"\"\"The hook scans the push range and blocks when a secret (always) or an identity/PII class (privacy-check on) appears.\"\"\"","+acceptance_criteria = \"The hook scans the push range and blocks when a secret (always) or an identity/PII class (privacy-check on) appears. With no interpreter at the runtime floor, it refuses the push, names the developer-setup install step, and neither scans below that floor nor skips the scan.\""," priority = \"M\""," verification = \"Test\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":228,"oldLines":7,"newStart":228,"newLines":7,"lines":[" hat_refs = [\"FIRST-RUN-ADOPTER\"]"," requirement = \"\"\"The onboarding and dev-setup templates shall scaffold and run to a green developer setup.\"\"\""," rationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-001 — a new contributor who cannot reach a working setup from the repo alone is blocked on whoever set it up last, and onboarding prose that is never executed drifts from the commands that work. A README checklist was rejected: nothing fails when it goes stale.\"\"\"","-acceptance_criteria = \"The scaffolded onboard/dev-setup scripts run to a green setup.\"","+acceptance_criteria = \"The scaffolded onboard/dev-setup scripts run to a green setup. When this repository's Windows developer setup has no interpreter at the runtime floor, its attended install operation offers one consent-first through an available provisioner, searches again after either response, and otherwise exits with the installation step; declining runs no provisioner.\""," priority = \"S\""," verification = \"Test\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":328,"oldLines":7,"newStart":328,"newLines":7,"lines":[" hat_refs = [\"CONSISTENCY\", \"CROSS-PLATFORM\"]"," requirement = \"\"\"The launchers at the repository root shall expose every declared runnable capability consistently to an interactive operator, to a direct caller naming one capability, and to automated discovery - from a single declaration, on Windows and POSIX alike.\"\"\""," rationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-001 - the evaluator's rungs make running the product never depend on recalling a command, and the capability set is declared once in docs/stack.ini rather than hard-wired and duplicated across the platform launchers. ONE OBLIGATION, not a menu specification: the row states the one capability-level decision - every declared capability is reachable, the same way, from one declaration, by three kinds of caller - because numbering, listing format, declaration grammar, fallback text and exit handling fail independently, which makes an enumeration of them a decomposition wearing a requirement's clothes. Those are LLR-047's and the acceptance's.\"\"\"","-acceptance_criteria = \"A machine listing prints one name-and-description line per declared capability in declaration order; a direct call naming a declared capability runs that capability's command and returns its exit code; the no-arg menu launches a stdin-selected capability non-interactively and does not hang on closed stdin; an absent or empty capability declaration prints guidance and exits 1; a declared description renders in both the menu and the listing; the platform launchers delegate to the one selector rather than carrying commands of their own; a fresh scaffold ships the selector and the delegate launchers. A no-argument launch runs its readiness step once from the repository root before the menu and, if the runtime remains missing, exits with guidance; a direct or discovery launch skips that step and any closing pause; and piped menu selection survives the readiness step.\"","+acceptance_criteria = \"A machine listing prints one name-and-description line per declared capability in declaration order; a direct call naming a declared capability runs that capability's command and returns its exit code; the no-arg menu launches a stdin-selected capability non-interactively and does not hang on closed stdin; an absent or empty capability declaration prints guidance and exits 1; a declared description renders in both the menu and the listing; the platform launchers delegate to the one selector rather than carrying commands of their own; a fresh scaffold ships the selector and the delegate launchers. A no-argument launch runs its readiness step once from the repository root before the menu and, if the runtime remains missing, exits with guidance; a direct or discovery launch skips that step and any closing pause; piped menu selection survives the readiness step; and a declared command using bare python to invoke the language runtime resolves to the floor-resolved interpreter on every supported platform, while a declared command using bare python3 resolves to it on POSIX.\""," priority = \"S\""," verification = \"Test\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-880\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-880\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-880\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\system-requirements.toml"]}}}
